WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.140
From once-iconic child stars&nbsp;
to European beauty queens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:09.360
2023 has seen the last of many great&nbsp;
TV, film, and video game actors.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:15.240
Lance Kerwin spent his childhood racking up&nbsp;
guest roles as plucky kids on '70s fare like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.640
Police Story, Cannon, and multiple after-school&nbsp;
specials. As he grew, he starred as relatable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:27.360
and sensitive teen James Hunter on the drama&nbsp;
James at 15, renamed James at 16 in 1978.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.860
Playing a realistic teenager made Kerwin&nbsp;
into a real-life teen idol in the late&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:38.100
1970s and early 1980s. He parlayed this&nbsp;
status into parts in the TV movie The Boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.780
Who Drank Too Much and the hit miniseries&nbsp;
adaptation of Stephen King's Salem's Lot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.960
in which he played lead&nbsp;
vampire resister Mark Petrie.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.880
"It wasn't a dream."

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.320
Kerwin bounced around TV for years before largely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.720
retiring from acting after an appearance in&nbsp;
1995's Outbreak. According to his daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:04.320
Kerwin died on January 24, 2023 in&nbsp;
San Clemente, California. He was 62.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:10.680
Earl Boen was a consummate character actor, highly&nbsp;
recognizable by his face, voice, and demeanor for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:16.740
any number of the nearly 300 projects he was&nbsp;
involved with from the mid 1970s to the 2010s.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:21.960
He was probably best known for his recurring role&nbsp;
across two decades' worth of Terminator movies: In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:27.000
the first three entries of the sci-fi franchise,&nbsp;
Boen played persistent criminal psychologist Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.480
Peter Silberman. Boen also co-starred in Alien&nbsp;
Nation, 9 to 5, and My Stepmother is an Alien.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.820
On the small screen, Boen enjoyed recurring&nbsp;
roles on Mama's Family, Scarecrow and Mrs. King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:44.040
and Webster. He also had an illustrious career as&nbsp;
a voice actor, contributing to animated projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:49.080
like Kim Possible, The New Batman Adventures,&nbsp;
Pinky and the Brain, and Clifford the Big Red Dog.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:54.240
On January 6, 2023, TMZ reported&nbsp;
that the character actor had died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.760
the previous day in Hawaii. A family friend told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.200
Variety that Boen had recently been&nbsp;
diagnosed with lung cancer. He was 81.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.300
An art student and beauty queen, screen&nbsp;
legend Gina Lollobrigida moved into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:10.860
acting in her native Italy just after&nbsp;
World War II. This was an explosively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.180
creative era for Italian cinema, and&nbsp;
Lollobrigida was a key part of it.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:20.760
She became a superstar in Europe and an&nbsp;
international sex symbol in the 1950s, headlining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:26.460
a run of Hollywood hits including The Hunchback of&nbsp;
Notre Dame, Beat the Devil, and Solomon and Sheba.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.140
She ultimately headed back to Italy, where she&nbsp;
starred in, wrote, and directed a number of films.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:37.320
Lollobrigida didn't act much after 1973, though&nbsp;
she did pop up on Falcon Crest and The Love Boat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:43.080
She filled her time by becoming a celebrated&nbsp;
photojournalist and a politician. In 2022 she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:48.780
ran for a seat in the Italian Senate. According to&nbsp;
NPR, Lollobrigida had leg surgery after she broke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:56.700
a thigh bone in a fall in September 2022. She&nbsp;
died in Rome on January 16, 2023 at the age of 95.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.380
Annie Wersching was a prolific actor,&nbsp;
booking roles on dozens of TV shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.340
throughout the 2000s, along with work in&nbsp;
the original The Last of Us video game.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.420
"I know where he's hiding."

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.520
"Like hell you do."

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.820
"Old warehouse in Area 5."

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.400
Wersching earned particular acclaim for&nbsp;
her performances as Julia Brasher on Bosch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.000
the Borg Queen on Star Trek: Picard,&nbsp;
and Emma Whitmore on Timeless.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:26.100
She further distinguished herself by appearing&nbsp;
in a number of fiercely beloved sci-fi, action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:31.080
and fantasy television series: Her first-ever&nbsp;
credit comes from an episode of Star Trek:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.300
Enterprise, and she later popped up on series&nbsp;
like Angel, Charmed, Supernatural, and Revolution.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.860
Viewers might also remember Wersching from The&nbsp;
Vampire Diaries, on which she played wicked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:47.580
vampire family matriarch Lily, or 24, which saw&nbsp;
her portray FBI agent Renee Walker. Wersching also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:52.860
portrayed duplicitous cult leader Leslie Dean on&nbsp;
the Marvel series Runaways. According to Deadline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.860 --> 00:04:01.140
doctors diagnosed Wersching with cancer in 2020.&nbsp;
She died on January 29, 2023, at the age of 45.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:07.020
In 1977, Adam Rich began a four-year run as&nbsp;
Nicholas, the youngest of the eight Bradford&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:12.360
children on Eight is Enough. Rich went on to enjoy&nbsp;
a number of guest roles on a variety of series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.540
including Silver Spoons, St.&nbsp;
Elsewhere, The Love Boat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:20.160
and The Six Million Dollar Man. Tabletop&nbsp;
role-playing game fans might also remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.860
him from the 1980s Dungeons &amp; Dragons animated&nbsp;
series, on which he voiced the magical Presto.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:31.620
In the 1990s, celebrated author and publisher&nbsp;
Dave Eggers recruited Rich for a massive prank:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.900
Eggers' magazine Might reported Rich's death. The&nbsp;
fictitious memorial tribute was so convincing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:44.100
genuine news outlets attempted to jump on the&nbsp;
story. Rich died on January 7, 2023. He was 54.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:48.780
Lisa Loring cemented her legacy at a&nbsp;
very early age when she portrayed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:53.340
iconic and enduring character of Wednesday&nbsp;
Addams. Loring was the first actor to ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:57.840
play the somber girl on screen, making&nbsp;
her mark in 1964's The Addams Family.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:02.580
This performance is still making waves, with&nbsp;
her frenetic dance with co-star Ted Cassidy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:07.620
becoming a meme in recent years. A breakout&nbsp;
child star, Loring acted only occasionally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:12.360
after The Addams Family ended, with appearances&nbsp;
on The Girl from U.N.C.L.E., Fantasy Island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.620
Barnaby Jones, and a long stint on As&nbsp;
the World Turns in the early 1980s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.400
Her final work came in the 2015&nbsp;
indie horror movie Doctor Spine.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.620
Loring's friend Laurie Jacobson reported&nbsp;
on Facebook that on January 25, 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:31.680
the actor suffered a severe stroke. She&nbsp;
died on January 28, at the age of 64.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:36.540
Cindy Williams was an icon of 1970s&nbsp;
entertainment. Following some due-paying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:40.980
with commercials and guest starring roles,&nbsp;
Williams landed big parts in major movies by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:45.900
two of the era's most important filmmakers.&nbsp;
She played Laurie in George Lucas' nostalgic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:50.460
blockbuster American Graffiti and Ann in&nbsp;
Francis Ford Coppola's The Conversation.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:54.960
A 1975 performance on Happy Days&nbsp;
led to Williams' most famous role:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.640
Shirley Feeney. Shirley and her friend Laverne&nbsp;
serve as intimidatingly older dates for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:04.440
show's teenage characters. Their episode proved&nbsp;
so popular that a Laverne &amp; Shirley spin-off hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:12.000
the air in 1976. By the 1977-1978 season, it&nbsp;
was the most-watched program on television.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.851
"I don't vo-de-oh-do-do."

00:06:15.851 --> 00:06:18.962
"You vo-de-oh-do-do."

00:06:18.962 --> 00:06:21.480
Williams died on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:26.760
January 25, 2023, following&nbsp;
a brief illness. She was 75.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:31.980
Melinda Dillon kicked off her acting career in a&nbsp;
big way by earning a Tony Award nomination for her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:37.740
performance in the original 1963 production of&nbsp;
Edward Albee's Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf?

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.040
In the '70s, she led the casts&nbsp;
of three classics of the era:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.480
Hal Ashby Woody Guthrie biopic, Bound&nbsp;
For Glory, the hockey comedy Slap Shot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.380
and Steven Spielberg's sci-fi smash&nbsp;
Close Encounters of the Third Kind

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:54.840
However, it wasn't until the 1980s that Dillon&nbsp;
landed her most iconic and enduring role:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:59.340
every year, millions of people watch her play&nbsp;
the Parker family's doting mother in perennial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:03.840
holiday favorite A Christmas Story. Dillon&nbsp;
followed that era-spanning hit with supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.520
turns in well-received movies like Harry and the&nbsp;
Hendersons, The Prince of Tides, and Magnolia.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:13.800
Twice nominated for Academy Awards, both for&nbsp;
Close Encounters of the Third Kind and Absence of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:21.300
Malice, Dillon was a giant of 20th century film.&nbsp;
She died on January 9, 2023, at the age of 83.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.840
Charles Kimbrough brought an air of&nbsp;
dignified authority to most of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:28.560
roles he played across five decades of&nbsp;
acting. He is perhaps most famous for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:33.180
portraying Jim Dial on Murphy Brown, an&nbsp;
upright and uptight veteran anchor — a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.540
role that brought Kimbrough an&nbsp;
Emmy Award nomination in 1990.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:41.040
In recent decades, Kimbrough introduced his&nbsp;
deep and serious voice to the world of cartoons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:45.780
portraying characters like Victor in Disney's&nbsp;
The Hunchback of Notre Dame and its spin-offs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:49.260
Mort Chalk in Recess, and Dr. Ficus on Dinosaurs.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.440
Kimbrough's voice also helped make&nbsp;
him a star earlier in his career:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:57.000
He was a two-time Tony Award nominee for his&nbsp;
work in big theatrical productions on Broadway.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:02.880
Among many notable performances, Kimbrough&nbsp;
co-starred in Company, Candide, and My Fair Lady

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.380
Kimbrough also came out of retirement to&nbsp;
reprise the role as Jim Dial on the 2018&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:15.240
Murphy Brown reboot. Kimbrough died on January&nbsp;
11, 2023, in Culver City, California. He was 86.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:19.980
Raquel Welch was among the most iconic and&nbsp;
glamorous movie stars of the 20th century.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:25.680
She made a big move into acting in 1966 with the&nbsp;
sci-fi classic Fantastic Voyage, in which she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:30.660
played a scientist who is shrunken down and sent&nbsp;
into a sick man's body to investigate his illness.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:34.860
That same year, Welch starred in the&nbsp;
prehistoric adventure One Million Years B.C.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:38.760
which saw her don a fur bikini. Images&nbsp;
of her in this unique garment became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:42.960
the cornerstone of the film's marketing&nbsp;
blitz and a legendary pin-up. Many vampy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:48.540
and showy roles followed in the 1960s and&nbsp;
1970s, with Bedazzled, The Three Musketeers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:53.460
and Myra Breckinridge. Her most notable recent&nbsp;
role came in Legally Blonde, in which she played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:56.940
the widow of a wealthy man whose murder&nbsp;
is one of the central points of the film.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:01.200
According to a statement provided by her&nbsp;
manager, the actor died on February 15,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.760
2023, following a short period&nbsp;
of illness. Welch was 82.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:12.660
In the 1970s and 1980s, Richard Belzer established&nbsp;
himself as a dark, acerbic, and deeply cynical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:17.400
wisecracker. That outsider stance, which saw&nbsp;
him deliver unapologetic social commentary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:22.500
informed many of Belzer's hosting gigs and&nbsp;
acting roles, particularly Detective John Munch.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:25.560
Belzer originated the character&nbsp;
on Homicide: Life on the Street,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.740
and went on to portray him on&nbsp;
Law &amp; Order and Law &amp; Order:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:33.960
Special Victims Unit until 2016. He also&nbsp;
brought the world-weary, droll-witted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:39.300
and curmudgeonly investigator to The Wire, 30&nbsp;
Rock, Arrested Development, and Sesame Street.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.740
Belzer and Munch shared a cultural background,&nbsp;
a complicated attitude about city life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:47.640
and an interest in conspiracy theories.&nbsp;
By bringing him to such vivid life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.680
the actor became a touchstone to generations&nbsp;
of TV-watchers. Belzer died on February 19,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:56.580
2023 at his home in France. He was 78.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:10:01.620
You might not recognize Ricou Browning by name,&nbsp;
but you definitely know his work. In a trio of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:07.320
films in the 1950s, he portrayed the iconic&nbsp;
Gill-Man, aka the Creature, in Universal's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:11.700
Creature from the Black Lagoon, Revenge of&nbsp;
the Creature, and The Creature Walks Among Us.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:16.740
Highly proficient in the sought-after skillset of&nbsp;
stunt performance and underwater cinematography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:22.080
Browning pulled off expressive and entirely&nbsp;
silent acting while completely submerged. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.520
played the Creature in the movies' many underwater&nbsp;
scenes, some of which are seriously lengthy.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.660
Browning continued to carve out a niche&nbsp;
in Hollywood as a creator and facilitator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:34.980
of waterlogged projects, directing the&nbsp;
underwater scenes in Caddyshack and Never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:39.480
Say Never Again, as well as co-creating&nbsp;
the friendly dolphin TV series Flipper.

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:42.960
Browning was part of a very small club&nbsp;
of actors who portrayed the titular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:47.280
monsters in Universal's beloved slew&nbsp;
of mid-century horror films. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.720
he was the last surviving original performer of&nbsp;
the "Universal monsters," as they're typically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:58.980
known. The actor and filmmaker died on February&nbsp;
27, 2023, at his home in Florida. He was 93.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:04.200
Lance Reddick brought star power and irresistible&nbsp;
energy to a series of high profile and cult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:09.000
projects over the years. His intensity and deep&nbsp;
character work often made them unforgettable.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:13.620
Reddick broke out on the HBO prison drama&nbsp;
Oz, where he played undercover narcotics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:17.940
officer Johnny Basil. He then appeared on&nbsp;
the celebrated drama The Wire as police&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:22.980
lieutenant Cedric Daniels. Reddick once again&nbsp;
played a complex authority figure on Fringe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:26.280
federal agent Phillip Broyles, head&nbsp;
of the titular paranormal office.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:31.140
Many more TV roles followed for Reddick,&nbsp;
including Deputy Chief Irving on Bosch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.840
Albert Wesker on Netflix's Resident Evil spin-off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.040
series, and deeply evil boss Christian&nbsp;
DeVille on Comedy Central's Corporate.

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:42.900
"How good to see you again so soon,&nbsp;
Mr. Wick. Shall I announce you?"

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.900
Film fans know him best as Charon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.500
the concierge-turned-sidekick of the&nbsp;
John Wick movies, while gamers will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:53.460
remember him for years to come as Commander&nbsp;
Zavala of the Destiny video game series.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:57.240
Reddick was discovered dead of natural&nbsp;
causes in his home outside Los Angeles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:01.920
on the morning of March 17,&nbsp;
2023. He was 60 years old.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:07.320
The '90s produced plenty of thoughtful action&nbsp;
movies and innovative indies about the seedier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:11.700
aspects of American life, and Tom Sizemore&nbsp;
was often a major part of that movement.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:16.800
After his breakthrough role as a Vietnam War-era&nbsp;
soldier on the TV drama China Beach earned him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:22.020
widespread attention, Sizemore appeared as a&nbsp;
DEA Agent in Point Break, a counter-terrorism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:27.360
expert in Passenger 57, a detective in True&nbsp;
Romance, Natural Born Killers, and The Relic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:33.360
and a sergeant in Saving Private Ryan. His career&nbsp;
ultimately came to encompass more than 200 roles.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:36.720
Sizemore collapsed at his home&nbsp;
in Los Angeles on February 19,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:43.320
2023. It was soon determined he'd suffered a brain&nbsp;
aneurysm. He died on March 3, at the age of 61.

